// The bone-ash cupel (OreProcessing, #722; README "Cupellation"): bone meal pressed into a dish in the
// grid (recipes/grid/cupel.json), fired like the game's clay in a pit kiln or a beehive kiln, then a
// smelting container in crucibulum's forge (Ore/Processing/BlockCupel.cs). Done, it is the cupel with
// its silver bead (BlockCupelBead.cs), broken with a hammer in the grid into litharge and metal bits.
// Single use. Kept a block, as the game's crucible is, for the smelting container class; ground
// stored, never placed. Marked disabled with the switch off.
{
	code: "cupel",
	classByType: {
		"cupel-raw": "Block",
		"cupel-fired": "seraphhorizons.BlockCupel",
